IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sgn-register`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), Part 11A, LAYER 1, fourth module: ss 386AG (the duty to investigate and obtain information), 386AH (to keep
-- information up to date), 386AI (to correct it), 386AIA (to ensure the register is up to date and correct), 386AJ (the controller's duty to provide
-- information) and 386AK (the controller's duty to provide a change of information).
--
-- THE PRESCRIBED THINGS. The time for compliance, the form, particulars and manner of a notice, the "other information", the frequency of the
-- ss 386AIA notice and the periods after which a notice or a notification is due are all left to regulations (ss 386AG(3), 386AH(2), 386AI(2), 386AIA(1), (2),
-- 386AJ(2), 386AK(2)). None is a source, so each is an input named for the fact; a prescribed period is a number of DAYS (assumed; fork F-AF4).
--
-- THE COUNTING. Every time limit is counted with the helper `s 386AF(8) timing: the act was done in time` (sgn-register.l4): JUST TRUE (done on or before the
-- last day), JUST FALSE (done late, or not done and the last day has passed), NOTHING (not done, and the last day has not passed).
-- Where a notice specifies its own time for compliance (ss 386AG(6), 386AH(6), 386AI(6), 386AIA(3)), the time is a DATE read from the notice, and the helper
-- is called with 0 days after that date (fork F-AG3).
--
-- THE OFFENCES. Each offence is a function over the failure to comply, which the caller states: an unmet element of an offence is JUST FALSE (split site (i),
-- fork F-AF6), the maximum penalty is a fine of $25,000 and no imprisonment (the text of each provision), and "officer who is in default" is the s 408(3)
-- phrase of another part, taken as an input (a seam).
--
-- READING A RESULT: see the header of sgn-application.l4.

§ `Section 386AG: the duty to investigate and obtain information`

-- (1): reasonable steps to find out and identify the registrable controllers.
-- No time is fixed and no offence follows a failure of (1) (the offence in (5) is for (2) or (3)), so a company that has not yet taken the steps is not shown to be in default.
-- src:25955 | 386AG.—(1) A company or foreign company must take reasonable
-- src:25956 | steps to find out and identify the registrable controllers of the
-- src:25957 | company or foreign company.
@ref s 386AG(1) (src:25955-25957)
GIVEN `the company or foreign company has taken reasonable steps to find out and identify its registrable controllers` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AG(1) the company or foreign company has complied with the duty to take reasonable steps` MEANS
    IF `the company or foreign company has taken reasonable steps to find out and identify its registrable controllers`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "reasonable" is not defined (undefined term) and the subsection fixes no time, so the steps not yet taken is not a failure the text names (fork F-AG1)

DECLARE `s 386AG act` IS ONE OF
    `s 386AG(1) take reasonable steps to find out and identify the registrable controllers`
    `s 386AG(2) give a notice to the person`
    `s 386AG(6) comply with the notice`

-- src:25955 | 386AG.—(1) A company or foreign company must take reasonable
-- src:25956 | steps to find out and identify the registrable controllers of the
-- src:25957 | company or foreign company.
@ref s 386AG(1) (src:25955-25957)
GIVEN `the company or foreign company` IS A Party
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 386AG act`
`s 386AG(1) a company or foreign company must take reasonable steps to find out and identify its registrable controllers` MEANS
    PARTY `the company or foreign company`
    MUST `s 386AG(1) take reasonable steps to find out and identify the registrable controllers`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 386AG(1) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY `the company or foreign company` BECAUSE "the company did not take reasonable steps to find out and identify its registrable controllers (s 386AG(1))" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md) [class: other; see notes]

-- (2): the two kinds of notice.
DECLARE `s 386AG(2) paragraph` IS ONE OF
    `s 386AG(2)(a) a notice to a person the company knows, or has reasonable grounds to believe, is a registrable controller`
    `s 386AG(2)(b) a notice to a person the company knows, or has reasonable grounds to believe, knows the identity of a registrable controller or is likely to have that knowledge`

-- src:25961 | (2) A company (A) or foreign company (A) —
-- src:25963 | (a) must give a notice to any person (B) whom A knows or has
-- src:25964 | reasonable grounds to believe is a registrable controller in
-- src:25965 | relation to A, requiring B —
-- src:25967 | (i) to state whether B is or is not a registrable controller
-- src:25968 | of A;
-- src:25970 | (ii) to state whether B knows or has reasonable grounds
-- src:25971 | to believe that any other person (C) is a registrable
-- src:25972 | controller of A or is likely to have that knowledge
-- src:25973 | and to give such particulars of C that are within B’s
-- src:25974 | knowledge; and
-- src:25976 | (iii) to provide such other information as may be
-- src:25977 | prescribed; and
-- src:25979 | (b) must give a notice to any person (D) whom A knows, or has
-- src:25980 | reasonable grounds to believe knows, the identity of a
-- src:25981 | person who is a registrable controller of A or is likely to
-- src:25982 | have that knowledge, requiring D —
-- src:25984 | (i) to state whether D knows or has reasonable grounds
-- src:25985 | to believe that any other person (E) is a registrable
-- src:25990 | controller of A or is likely to have that knowledge
-- src:25991 | and to give such particulars of E that are within D’s
-- src:25992 | knowledge; and
-- src:25994 | (ii) to provide such other information as may be
-- src:25995 | prescribed.
@ref s 386AG(2) (src:25961-25995)
GIVEN `the company or foreign company knows, or has reasonable grounds to believe, that the person is a registrable controller` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company or foreign company knows, or has reasonable grounds to believe, that the person knows the identity of a registrable controller or is likely to have that knowledge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all the information that the notice would require was previously provided by the person or by a registered corporate service provider on the person's behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AG(2) the company or foreign company must give a notice to the person` MEANS
    IF `s 386AG(4) subsection (2) requires the company or foreign company to give notice in respect of the information` `all the information that the notice would require was previously provided by the person or by a registered corporate service provider on the person's behalf` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, in s 386AG(4))
    ELSE (IF `the company or foreign company knows, or has reasonable grounds to believe, that the person is a registrable controller`
             OR `the company or foreign company knows, or has reasonable grounds to believe, that the person knows the identity of a registrable controller or is likely to have that knowledge`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (2) speaks of "any person (B) whom A knows or has reasonable grounds to believe is a registrable controller" and "any person (D) whom A knows, or has reasonable grounds to believe knows, the identity of a person who is a registrable controller"; another person is outside both limits

-- What each notice must require of its addressee: (a) requires (i), (ii) and (iii); (b) requires (i) and (ii) of its own list.
-- src:25961 | (2) A company (A) or foreign company (A) —
-- src:25963 | (a) must give a notice to any person (B) whom A knows or has
-- src:25964 | reasonable grounds to believe is a registrable controller in
-- src:25965 | relation to A, requiring B —
-- src:25967 | (i) to state whether B is or is not a registrable controller
-- src:25968 | of A;
-- src:25970 | (ii) to state whether B knows or has reasonable grounds
-- src:25971 | to believe that any other person (C) is a registrable
-- src:25972 | controller of A or is likely to have that knowledge
-- src:25973 | and to give such particulars of C that are within B’s
-- src:25974 | knowledge; and
-- src:25976 | (iii) to provide such other information as may be
-- src:25977 | prescribed; and
-- src:25979 | (b) must give a notice to any person (D) whom A knows, or has
-- src:25980 | reasonable grounds to believe knows, the identity of a
-- src:25981 | person who is a registrable controller of A or is likely to
-- src:25982 | have that knowledge, requiring D —
-- src:25984 | (i) to state whether D knows or has reasonable grounds
-- src:25985 | to believe that any other person (E) is a registrable
-- src:25990 | controller of A or is likely to have that knowledge
-- src:25991 | and to give such particulars of E that are within D’s
-- src:25992 | knowledge; and
-- src:25994 | (ii) to provide such other information as may be
-- src:25995 | prescribed.
@ref s 386AG(2) (src:25961-25995)
GIVEN paragraph IS A `s 386AG(2) paragraph`
      `the notice requires the addressee to state whether the addressee is or is not a registrable controller` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice requires the addressee to state whether the addressee knows or has reasonable grounds to believe that any other person is a registrable controller or is likely to have that knowledge, and to give such particulars of that person as are within the addressee's knowledge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice requires the addressee to provide such other information as may be prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AG(2) the notice requires what the paragraph requires` MEANS
    JUST (CONSIDER paragraph
          WHEN `s 386AG(2)(a) a notice to a person the company knows, or has reasonable grounds to believe, is a registrable controller` THEN
              `the notice requires the addressee to state whether the addressee is or is not a registrable controller`
              AND `the notice requires the addressee to state whether the addressee knows or has reasonable grounds to believe that any other person is a registrable controller or is likely to have that knowledge, and to give such particulars of that person as are within the addressee's knowledge`
              AND `the notice requires the addressee to provide such other information as may be prescribed`
          WHEN `s 386AG(2)(b) a notice to a person the company knows, or has reasonable grounds to believe, knows the identity of a registrable controller or is likely to have that knowledge` THEN
              `the notice requires the addressee to state whether the addressee knows or has reasonable grounds to believe that any other person is a registrable controller or is likely to have that knowledge, and to give such particulars of that person as are within the addressee's knowledge`
              AND `the notice requires the addressee to provide such other information as may be prescribed`)   -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question): "must give a notice ... requiring B — (i) ...; (ii) ...; and (iii) ..." and "requiring D — (i) ...; and (ii) ..."; a notice that leaves one item out is not the notice the paragraph describes

-- (3)(a) and (b): the content of the notice. (c): when it must be given.
-- src:25999 | (3) A notice mentioned in subsection (2) —
-- src:26001 | (a) must state that the addressee must comply with the notice
-- src:26002 | not later than the time prescribed for compliance;
-- src:26004 | (b) must be in such form, contain such particulars and be sent
-- src:26005 | in such manner, as may be prescribed; and
@ref s 386AG(3)(a) and (b) (src:25999-26005)
GIVEN `the notice states that the addressee must comply with the notice not later than the time prescribed for compliance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is in the prescribed form, contains the prescribed particulars and is sent in the prescribed manner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AG(3)(a) and (b) the notice is as the subsection requires` MEANS
    JUST (   `the notice states that the addressee must comply with the notice not later than the time prescribed for compliance`
         AND `the notice is in the prescribed form, contains the prescribed particulars and is sent in the prescribed manner`)   -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question): "A notice mentioned in subsection (2) (a) must state that the addressee must comply ... (b) must be in such form, contain such particulars and be sent in such manner, as may be prescribed"

