-- src:26011 | that subsection.
@ref s 386AG(3)(c) (src:26007-26011)
GIVEN `the company or foreign company has given the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the company or foreign company gave the notice` IS A DATE
      `the day the company or foreign company first knew, or first had reasonable grounds to believe, that there exists a person to whom a notice must be given under subsection (2)` IS A DATE
      `the prescribed period, in days` IS A NUMBER
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AG(3)(c) the company or foreign company has given the notice in time` MEANS
    `s 386AF(8) timing: the act was done in time` `the company or foreign company has given the notice` `the day the company or foreign company gave the notice` `the day the company or foreign company first knew, or first had reasonable grounds to believe, that there exists a person to whom a notice must be given under subsection (2)` `the prescribed period, in days` `the date asked`   -- FALSE-kind where late ("must be given within such period as may be prescribed after the company or foreign company first knows ...": a period the text fixes in its own words: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a)); NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording) while the period has not run out

-- The duty of (2) with the time of (3)(c), as a regulative rule: the prescribed period is the number of days.
-- src:26007 | (c) must be given within such period as may be prescribed
-- src:26008 | after the company or foreign company first knows the
-- src:26009 | existence of, or first has reasonable grounds to believe that
-- src:26010 | there exists, a person to whom a notice must be given under
-- src:26011 | that subsection.
@ref s 386AG(3)(c) (src:26007-26011)
GIVEN `the company or foreign company` IS A Party
      `the prescribed period, in days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 386AG act`
`s 386AG(2) and (3)(c) a company or foreign company must give the notice within the prescribed period after it first knows` MEANS
    PARTY `the company or foreign company`
    MUST `s 386AG(2) give a notice to the person`
    WITHIN `the prescribed period, in days`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the company or foreign company` BECAUSE "the company did not give the notice within the prescribed period after it first knew of a person to whom a notice must be given (s 386AG(2), (3)(c), (5))"


