§ `Section 386AH: the duty to keep information up to date`

-- (7): when a relevant change occurs ("occurs if": a failed "if" is the text's no, marginal reading (a)).
-- src:26119 | (7) For the purposes of this section, a relevant change occurs if —
-- src:26121 | (a) a person ceases to be a registrable controller in relation to
-- src:26122 | the company or foreign company, as the case may be; or
-- src:26124 | (b) any other change occurs as a result of which the particulars
-- src:26125 | of the registrable controller in the company’s or foreign
-- src:26126 | company’s register of controllers are incorrect or
-- src:26127 | incomplete.
@ref s 386AH(7) (src:26119-26127)
GIVEN `a person ceases to be a registrable controller in relation to the company or foreign company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any other change occurs as a result of which the particulars of the registrable controller in the register of controllers are incorrect or incomplete` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AH(7) a relevant change occurs` MEANS
    IF    `a person ceases to be a registrable controller in relation to the company or foreign company`
       OR `any other change occurs as a result of which the particulars of the registrable controller in the register of controllers are incorrect or incomplete`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (a failed "if", marginal reading (a)): "For the purposes of this section, a relevant change occurs if — (a) ...; or (b) ..."

-- (1) and (4): the duty to give notice to the registrable controller.
-- src:26056 | 386AH.—(1) If a company or foreign company knows or has
-- src:26057 | reasonable grounds to believe that a relevant change has occurred in
-- src:26058 | the particulars of a registrable controller that are stated in the
-- src:26059 | company’s or foreign company’s register of controllers, the company
-- src:26060 | or foreign company must give notice to the registrable controller —
-- src:26062 | (a) to confirm whether or not the change has occurred; and
-- src:26064 | (b) if the change has occurred —
-- src:26066 | (i) to state the date of the change; and
-- src:26068 | (ii) to provide the particulars of the change.
@ref s 386AH(1) (src:26056-26068)
GIVEN `the company or foreign company knows or has reasonable grounds to believe that a relevant change has occurred in the particulars of a registrable controller that are stated in its register of controllers` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all the information that the notice would require was previously provided by the registrable controller or by a registered corporate service provider on the registrable controller's behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AH(1) the company or foreign company must give notice to the registrable controller` MEANS
    IF `s 386AH(4) subsection (1) requires the company or foreign company to give notice in respect of the information` `all the information that the notice would require was previously provided by the registrable controller or by a registered corporate service provider on the registrable controller's behalf` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, in s 386AH(4))
    ELSE (IF `the company or foreign company knows or has reasonable grounds to believe that a relevant change has occurred in the particulars of a registrable controller that are stated in its register of controllers`
          THEN JUST TRUE
