GIVEN `the addressee fails to comply with the notice within the time specified in the notice for compliance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 386AI(6) the most the addressee may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 386AI(6) the addressee is guilty of the offence` `the addressee fails to comply with the notice within the time specified in the notice for compliance` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (Penalty OF 25000, 0, FALSE, FALSE)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty

§ `Section 386AIA: the duty to ensure the information in the register is up to date and correct`

-- (6): when a relevant change occurs ("occurs if": marginal reading (a)).
-- src:26234 | (6) For the purposes of this section, a relevant change occurs if —
-- src:26236 | (a) the registrable controller ceases to be one in relation to the
-- src:26237 | company or foreign company, as the case may be; or
-- src:26239 | (b) any other change occurs as a result of which the particulars
-- src:26240 | of the registrable controller stated in the company’s or
-- src:26241 | foreign company’s register of controllers are incorrect or
-- src:26242 | incomplete.
@ref s 386AIA(6) (src:26234-26242)
GIVEN `the registrable controller ceases to be one in relation to the company or foreign company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any other change occurs as a result of which the particulars of the registrable controller stated in the register of controllers are incorrect or incomplete` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AIA(6) a relevant change occurs` MEANS
    IF    `the registrable controller ceases to be one in relation to the company or foreign company`
       OR `any other change occurs as a result of which the particulars of the registrable controller stated in the register of controllers are incorrect or incomplete`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (a failed "if", marginal reading (a)): "For the purposes of this section, a relevant change occurs if — (a) ...; or (b) ..."

-- (1): the notice at the prescribed frequency, to each registrable controller whose particulars are in the register, for both purposes.
-- src:26191 | 386AIA.—(1) A company or foreign company must, at the
-- src:26192 | prescribed frequency, give a notice to each registrable controller
-- src:26193 | whose particulars are stated in the company’s or foreign company’s
-- src:26194 | register of controllers for the following purposes:
-- src:26196 | (a) to require the registrable controller to confirm whether or
-- src:26197 | not a relevant change has occurred and, if the change has
-- src:26198 | occurred, to —
-- src:26200 | (i) state the date of the change; and
-- src:26202 | (ii) provide the particulars of the change;
-- src:26204 | (b) to require the registrable controller to confirm whether the
-- src:26205 | stated particulars of the registrable controller are correct
-- src:26206 | and, if not, to provide the correct particulars.
@ref s 386AIA(1) (src:26191-26206)
GIVEN `the notice requires the registrable controller to confirm whether or not a relevant change has occurred and, if it has, to state the date of the change and provide the particulars of the change` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice requires the registrable controller to confirm whether the stated particulars are correct and, if not, to provide the correct particulars` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AIA(1) the notice serves the purposes the subsection lists` MEANS
    JUST (   `the notice requires the registrable controller to confirm whether or not a relevant change has occurred and, if it has, to state the date of the change and provide the particulars of the change`
         AND `the notice requires the registrable controller to confirm whether the stated particulars are correct and, if not, to provide the correct particulars`)   -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question): "give a notice ... for the following purposes: (a) ...; (b) ..." (both purposes: fork F-AIA1)

-- The frequency is prescribed; it is read as the most days that may pass between one notice and the next (fork F-AIA2). The first notice has no time stated.
-- src:26191 | 386AIA.—(1) A company or foreign company must, at the
-- src:26192 | prescribed frequency, give a notice to each registrable controller
-- src:26193 | whose particulars are stated in the company’s or foreign company’s
-- src:26194 | register of controllers for the following purposes:
@ref s 386AIA(1) (src:26191-26194)
GIVEN `the company or foreign company has given the next notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the company or foreign company gave the next notice` IS A DATE
      `the day the company or foreign company gave the previous notice` IS A DATE
      `the prescribed frequency, in days` IS A NUMBER
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AIA(1) the company or foreign company has given the next notice at the prescribed frequency` MEANS
    `s 386AF(8) timing: the act was done in time` `the company or foreign company has given the next notice` `the day the company or foreign company gave the next notice` `the day the company or foreign company gave the previous notice` `the prescribed frequency, in days` `the date asked`   -- FALSE-kind where late ("must, at the prescribed frequency, give a notice": a period the text fixes in its own words, once the frequency is stated: ruling (a)); NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording) while the frequency has not run out

DECLARE `s 386AIA act` IS ONE OF
    `s 386AIA(1) give a notice to each registrable controller`
    `s 386AIA(3) comply with the notice`

-- src:26191 | 386AIA.—(1) A company or foreign company must, at the
-- src:26192 | prescribed frequency, give a notice to each registrable controller
-- src:26193 | whose particulars are stated in the company’s or foreign company’s
-- src:26194 | register of controllers for the following purposes:
@ref s 386AIA(1) (src:26191-26194)
GIVEN `the company or foreign company` IS A Party
      `the prescribed frequency, in days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 386AIA act`
`s 386AIA(1) a company or foreign company must give a notice to each registrable controller at the prescribed frequency` MEANS
    PARTY `the company or foreign company`
    MUST `s 386AIA(1) give a notice to each registrable controller`
    WITHIN `the prescribed frequency, in days`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the company or foreign company` BECAUSE "the company did not give the notice to the registrable controller at the prescribed frequency (s 386AIA(1), (4))"

-- (2): what the notice must state, and its form.
-- src:26211 | (2) The notice mentioned in subsection (1) must —
-- src:26213 | (a) state that the addressee must comply with the notice not
-- src:26214 | later than the time specified for compliance (which must be
-- src:26215 | the prescribed time); and
-- src:26217 | (b) be in such form, contain such particulars and be sent in
-- src:26218 | such manner, as may be prescribed.
@ref s 386AIA(2) (src:26211-26218)
GIVEN `the notice states that the addressee must comply with the notice not later than the time specified for compliance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time specified for compliance is the prescribed time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is in the prescribed form, contains the prescribed particulars and is sent in the prescribed manner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AIA(2) the notice is as the subsection requires` MEANS
    JUST (   `the notice states that the addressee must comply with the notice not later than the time specified for compliance`
         AND `the time specified for compliance is the prescribed time`
         AND `the notice is in the prescribed form, contains the prescribed particulars and is sent in the prescribed manner`)   -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question): "The notice mentioned in subsection (1) must — (a) state that the addressee must comply with the notice not later than the time specified for compliance (which must be the prescribed time); and (b) be in such form, contain such particulars and be sent in such manner, as may be prescribed"

-- (3): the addressee must comply no later than the time specified.
-- src:26220 | (3) An addressee of a notice under subsection (1) must comply with
-- src:26221 | the notice no later than the time specified in the notice for
-- src:26222 | compliance.
@ref s 386AIA(3) (src:26220-26222)
GIVEN `the addressee has complied with the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the addressee complied with the notice` IS A DATE
      `the date specified in the notice by which the addressee must comply` IS A DATE
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AIA(3) the addressee has complied with the notice no later than the time specified` MEANS
    `s 386AF(8) timing: the act was done in time` `the addressee has complied with the notice` `the day the addressee complied with the notice` `the date specified in the notice by which the addressee must comply` 0 `the date asked`   -- FALSE-kind where late ("must comply with the notice no later than the time specified in the notice for compliance": a period the text fixes in its own words: ruling (a)); NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording) while the time has not run out

-- src:26220 | (3) An addressee of a notice under subsection (1) must comply with
-- src:26221 | the notice no later than the time specified in the notice for
-- src:26222 | compliance.
@ref s 386AIA(3) (src:26220-26222)
GIVEN `the addressee` IS A Party
      `the number of days the notice specifies for compliance` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 386AIA act`
`s 386AIA(3) an addressee must comply with the notice no later than the time specified in it` MEANS
    PARTY `the addressee`
    MUST `s 386AIA(3) comply with the notice`
    WITHIN `the number of days the notice specifies for compliance`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the addressee` BECAUSE "the addressee did not comply with the notice no later than the time specified in it (s 386AIA(3), (5))"

-- (4) and (5): the offences.
-- src:26224 | (4) If a company or foreign company fails to comply with
-- src:26225 | subsection (1) or (2), the company or foreign company, and every
-- src:26226 | officer of the company or foreign company who is in default, shall
-- src:26227 | each be guilty of an offence and shall each be liable on conviction to a
-- src:26228 | fine not exceeding $25,000.
