§ `Section 386AJ: the controller's duty to provide information`

-- (1) and (3): who must notify. A person who knows or ought reasonably to know that the person is a registrable controller must notify; "need not" if a notice under s 386AG(2) was complied with in time.
-- src:26248 | 386AJ.—(1) A person who knows or ought reasonably to know
-- src:26249 | that the person is a registrable controller in relation to a company or
-- src:26250 | foreign company must —
-- src:26252 | (a) notify the company or foreign company (as the case may
-- src:26253 | be) that the person is a registrable controller in relation to
-- src:26254 | the company or foreign company;
-- src:26259 | (b) state the date, to the best of the person’s knowledge, on
-- src:26260 | which the person became a registrable controller in relation
-- src:26261 | to the company or foreign company; and
-- src:26263 | (c) provide such other information as may be prescribed.
@ref s 386AJ(1) (src:26248-26263)
GIVEN `the person knows or ought reasonably to know that the person is a registrable controller in relation to the company or foreign company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has received a notice from the company or foreign company under section 386AG(2) and has complied with the requirements of the notice within the time specified in the notice for compliance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AJ(1) the person must notify the company or foreign company` MEANS
    IF `s 386AJ(3) subsection (1) requires the person to comply` `the person has received a notice from the company or foreign company under section 386AG(2) and has complied with the requirements of the notice within the time specified in the notice for compliance` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, in s 386AJ(3))
    ELSE (IF `the person knows or ought reasonably to know that the person is a registrable controller in relation to the company or foreign company`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (1) speaks of "A person who knows or ought reasonably to know that the person is a registrable controller"; another person is outside the limit

-- (1) and (2): the three things, and the time.
-- src:26267 | (2) The person mentioned in subsection (1) must comply with the
-- src:26268 | requirements of that subsection within such period as may be
-- src:26269 | prescribed after the date on which that person first knew or ought
-- src:26270 | reasonably to have known that that person was a registrable
-- src:26271 | controller.
@ref s 386AJ(2) (src:26267-26271)
GIVEN `the person has notified the company or foreign company that the person is a registrable controller` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has stated the date, to the best of the person's knowledge, on which the person became a registrable controller` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has provided such other information as may be prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the person completed what subsection (1) requires` IS A DATE
      `the day the person first knew or ought reasonably to have known that the person was a registrable controller` IS A DATE
      `the prescribed period, in days` IS A NUMBER
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AJ(1) and (2) the person has complied with the requirements in time` MEANS
    `s 386AF(8) timing: the act was done in time`
        (   `the person has notified the company or foreign company that the person is a registrable controller`
        AND `the person has stated the date, to the best of the person's knowledge, on which the person became a registrable controller`
        AND `the person has provided such other information as may be prescribed`)
        `the day the person completed what subsection (1) requires` `the day the person first knew or ought reasonably to have known that the person was a registrable controller` `the prescribed period, in days` `the date asked`   -- FALSE-kind where late ("must comply with the requirements of that subsection within such period as may be prescribed after the date on which that person first knew or ought reasonably to have known": a period the text fixes in its own words: ruling (a)); NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording) while the period has not run out

DECLARE `s 386AJ act` IS ONE OF
    `s 386AJ(1) notify the company or foreign company, state the date and provide the other information`

-- src:26267 | (2) The person mentioned in subsection (1) must comply with the
-- src:26268 | requirements of that subsection within such period as may be
-- src:26269 | prescribed after the date on which that person first knew or ought
-- src:26270 | reasonably to have known that that person was a registrable
-- src:26271 | controller.
