      `the person has received a notice from the company or foreign company under section 386AH(1) and has complied with the requirements of the notice within the time specified in the notice for compliance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AK(1) the person must notify the company or foreign company of the relevant change` MEANS
    IF `s 386AK(3) subsection (1) requires the person to comply` `the person has received a notice from the company or foreign company under section 386AH(1) and has complied with the requirements of the notice within the time specified in the notice for compliance` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, in s 386AK(3))
    ELSE (IF `the person is a registrable controller in relation to the company or foreign company who knows, or ought reasonably to know, that a relevant change has occurred in the prescribed particulars of the registrable controller`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (1) speaks of "A person who is a registrable controller ... who knows, or ought reasonably to know, that a relevant change has occurred"; another person is outside the limit

-- (1) and (2): the notification (the date, the particulars) and the time.
-- src:26305 | (2) The person mentioned in subsection (1) must comply with the
-- src:26306 | requirements of that subsection within such period as may be
-- src:26307 | prescribed after the date on which that person first knew or ought
-- src:26308 | reasonably to have known of the relevant change.
@ref s 386AK(2) (src:26305-26308)
GIVEN `the person has notified the company or foreign company of the relevant change, stating the date that the change occurred and providing the particulars of the change` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the person notified the company or foreign company of the relevant change` IS A DATE
      `the day the person first knew or ought reasonably to have known of the relevant change` IS A DATE
      `the prescribed period, in days` IS A NUMBER
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AK(1) and (2) the person has notified the company or foreign company of the relevant change in time` MEANS
    `s 386AF(8) timing: the act was done in time` `the person has notified the company or foreign company of the relevant change, stating the date that the change occurred and providing the particulars of the change` `the day the person notified the company or foreign company of the relevant change` `the day the person first knew or ought reasonably to have known of the relevant change` `the prescribed period, in days` `the date asked`   -- FALSE-kind where late ("within such period as may be prescribed after the date on which that person first knew or ought reasonably to have known of the relevant change": a period the text fixes in its own words: ruling (a)); NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording) while the period has not run out

DECLARE `s 386AK act` IS ONE OF
    `s 386AK(1) notify the company or foreign company of the relevant change, stating the date and providing the particulars`

-- src:26305 | (2) The person mentioned in subsection (1) must comply with the
-- src:26306 | requirements of that subsection within such period as may be
-- src:26307 | prescribed after the date on which that person first knew or ought
-- src:26308 | reasonably to have known of the relevant change.
@ref s 386AK(2) (src:26305-26308)
GIVEN `the person` IS A Party
      `the prescribed period, in days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 386AK act`
`s 386AK(1) and (2) a registrable controller must notify the company or foreign company of a relevant change within the prescribed period` MEANS
    PARTY `the person`
    MUST `s 386AK(1) notify the company or foreign company of the relevant change, stating the date and providing the particulars`
    WITHIN `the prescribed period, in days`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the person` BECAUSE "the person did not notify the company of the relevant change within the prescribed period (s 386AK(1), (2), (4))"


-- src:26315 | (3) A person need not comply with the requirements of
-- src:26316 | subsection (1) if the person has received a notice from the
-- src:26317 | company or foreign company under section 386AH(1) and has
-- src:26318 | complied with the requirements of the notice within the time
-- src:26319 | specified in the notice for compliance.
@ref s 386AK(3) (src:26315-26319)
GIVEN `the person has received a notice from the company or foreign company under section 386AH(1) and has complied with the requirements of the notice within the time specified in the notice for compliance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AK(3) subsection (1) requires the person to comply` MEANS
    IF `the person has received a notice from the company or foreign company under section 386AH(1) and has complied with the requirements of the notice within the time specified in the notice for compliance`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person need not comply with the requirements of subsection (1) if the person has received a notice from the company or foreign company under section 386AH(1) and has complied with the requirements of the notice within the time specified in the notice for compliance"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (3) says only when the other subsection does not require it; in any other case it is silent

-- (4): the offence.
-- src:26323 | (4) Any person who fails to comply with subsection (1) or (2) shall
-- src:26324 | be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:26325 | exceeding $25,000.
@ref s 386AK(4) (src:26323-26325)
GIVEN `the person fails to comply with subsection (1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AK(4) the person is guilty of the offence` MEANS
    IF `the person fails to comply with subsection (1) or (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question; split site (i)): "Any person who fails to comply with subsection (1) or (2) shall be guilty of an offence"

-- src:26323 | (4) Any person who fails to comply with subsection (1) or (2) shall
-- src:26324 | be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:26325 | exceeding $25,000.
@ref s 386AK(4) (src:26323-26325)
GIVEN `the person fails to comply with subsection (1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 386AK(4) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 386AK(4) the person is guilty of the offence` `the person fails to comply with subsection (1) or (2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (Penalty OF 25000, 0, FALSE, FALSE)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty
